> Inspect the actual experiment results

Every one of the60 original episode lengths is shown. A1000-step value denotes truncation; the final ten episodes and the original seeded greedy checks are retained. The saved1536-weight tensor is the fitted model.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/linear_fa_results.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){auto archive=dm::nn::load_npz("build/linear_fa_source.npz");auto get=[&](const std::string& name){auto it=std::find_if(archive.begin(),archive.end(),[&](const auto& p){return p.first==name;});if(it==archive.end())throw std::runtime_error("missing source series "+name);return it->second.to_vector<double>();};auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();{auto values=get("steps");std::vector<double>x;x.resize(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),1.);plot.lines(x,values,"steps to goal or limit",{37,99,235});}plot.title("linear fa source results").x_label("Training episode (one based)").y_label("Episode steps").size(1150,650).save_svg("build/linear_fa_results.svg");}
